 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Hey, nice to hear from you. How are things at home? Generally, people in English speaking countries put the date line at the top of date line, so it's easy to spot. Does that work for you? Then lead with the date, and follow it with the time. People read from right to left, so it feels natural. Email is fine. A clear subject line helps, especially if the folder name is bland. That's a lovely touch, if she still does them. Lots of older people do, and it' very nice. Just use the name of the person and a link to the calendar event. People can add themselves to the calendar if they want to.",
